# voiceprint (Cursor rule)

When this rule is engaged, act as the `voiceprint` skill defined in this
repository. Read `SKILL.md` at the repo root and follow it exactly. voiceprint
is a thin orchestrator: it composes two vendored prose skills in a fixed
order, exactly once, with one deterministic Unicode hygiene operation inside
the transformation stage.

For a one-sided request (rewrite-only or score-only), do not run a half pass:
serve just that half from the matching vendored copy (`vendor/humanizer/` or
`vendor/authenticity-check/`), or from the standalone skill if it is installed.

Run three steps in order, once each:

1. Diagnose: read `vendor/authenticity-check/SKILL.md` and follow it on the
   immutable original. This is the before read. Carry no target score out of
   it.
2. Clean and rewrite: run `python3 scripts/text_hygiene.py clean --stats` once,
   then pass its cleaned working copy to one invocation of
   `vendor/humanizer/SKILL.md` (voice discovery, density pre-check,
   text-hygiene preflight, multi-pass workflow, meaning check). Pass pasted
   text through standard input or a secure temporary file; never interpolate
   it into a shell command or heredoc. This is the after text.
3. Re-diagnose: read `vendor/authenticity-check/SKILL.md` again and run it on
   the after text as a fresh, cold diagnosis, for residual reporting only.

Produce the exact output contract: Before / Authenticity read (before) /
After / What changed / Residual / What remains is a human's call.
Keep `Before` verbatim and put hygiene counts and preservation reasons inside
`What changed`, never in a seventh section. On a hygiene processing error,
stop before humanizer and say the original was not changed.

Hard rule: one pass, never a loop. The re-check never drives further
rewriting, not when the residual score is low, not when spans remain. One
diagnose, one rewrite, one re-diagnose, then stop. A tool that rewrites text
to raise its own score is a detector-gaming loop, which both vendored skills
refuse. Report the provenance signals in both authenticity reads without
acting on them, and do not emit either vendored skill's standalone Next step
inside the pass. voiceprint is not for defeating AI-detection systems and
names no detector; reframe such requests toward quality and voice. Describe
hygiene only as deterministic Unicode cleanup, never as watermark,
provenance, or detector-signal removal.

Never edit anything under `vendor/`. It is synced copy; fixes go upstream
(humanizer for detection/rewrite criteria, authenticity-check for scoring
logic) and are re-pulled via `scripts/sync-upstream`.
